From 4e7bce2f5ba3684c17ee87f170b7c8fbdc0f9e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:37:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] feat(deploy): check fake instances every second in the
 Kubernetes trial

The compose overlay for the fake launcher checks instances every
second so that an instance that exits is noticed right away; the
Kubernetes trial patch kept the 10 second default and the docs did
not say how to exercise an instance loss there at all.

fake-runtime-patch.yaml now sets FORGEMESH_INSTANCE_CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS
to 1 like the overlay, and the README shows how to make an instance
exit with POST /fake/exit from inside the control plane container:
the network policies only let the gateway reach the instance ports,
and the gateway does not forward that path.

Validated on kind: after the README command the service was Degraded
(InstanceLost) within half a second and Ready on a new instance less
than two seconds later, and the control plane counted one lost
instance and one redeploy.
